of future projects is closely related to historical quantities, and project types are often related
to the host country, we can divide them into: host country's advantageous projects, disadvanta-
geous projects, and neutral projects. For advantageous and disadvantageous projects, we con-




                                                          型
sider that the host country effect may lead to an increase in advantageous projects and a de-
crease in disadvantageous projects, so we choose the SARIMAX model, which takes into ac-




                                                        模
count exogenous variables. Neutral projects are often not affected by the host country effect,
so the ARIMA model is used for prediction. In addition, we have used the same method to




