7 The Solution of Problem 3

7.1 Former host effect and Subsequent host effect.

     In the previous experiments, we identified the "former host effect" and the "subsequent
host effect." The "former host effect" refers to the phenomenon where a country, upon learn-
ing that it will host the upcoming Olympic Games, performs above its average level in the




                                                                 型
subsequent Olympic Games until the country hosts its own Olympic Games. The "subsequent
host effect" refers to the significant decline in the host country's performance in the following




                                                           模
Olympic Games, indicating that the competitive sports strength not only reverts from the
"home advantage" to the normal level, but may also drop one or more levels below the nor-


                                                   学
mal level. For example, in our previous prediction, Japan, as the host of the 2021 Olympic
Games, showed an improvement in performance during the 2016 Rio Olympics. Similarly, as
                                             数
the host of the 2024 Olympics, France experienced a certain degree of performance decline in
the 2028 Olympic Games.
